    "artifacts/design.md": {
      "encoding": "text",
      "content": "# Copy contract\n\nCopy the exact approved JSON array from artifacts/input.json to artifacts/output.json. Preserve values and order. Do not mutate the input. Missing input or contents differing from the approved input stop without an output. No retry or fallback is allowed. The fictional example-copy tool performs exactly one call within the approved resource limits. Runtime is fictional-copy-1 and platform is fictional. There are no environment variables, random choices, or concurrent operations.\n"
    },
    "artifacts/input.json": {
      "encoding": "json",
      "content": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ]
    },
    "artifacts/output.json": {
      "encoding": "json",
      "content": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ]
    },
    "artifacts/overview.md": {
      "encoding": "text",
      "content": "# Fictional copy project\n\nOne copy step. No real approval or execution is represented.\n"
    },
    "artifacts/spec.md": {
      "encoding": "text",
      "content": "# Copy vector\n\n### Requirement: preserve-vector\n\nThe step SHALL copy the vector without changing its values or order.\n\n#### Scenario: Three values\n\nWHEN the input is [1, 2, 3],\nTHEN the output is [1, 2, 3] and the input is unchanged.\n"
    },
    "artifacts/tasks.md": {
      "encoding": "text",
      "content": "# Fictional tasks\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Copy the approved vector and check exact JSON equality.\n\nThis preserved task definition precedes implementation. Completion is recorded separately in acceptance and project state.\n"
    },
    "artifacts/work.txt": {
